<title>USA: U.S. Spring/White Wheat - Bids mostly lower.</title>
<headline>U.S. Spring/White Wheat - Bids mostly lower.</headline>
<dateline>CHICAGO 1996-10-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bids for dark northern spring and white wheat were mostly lower and farmer selling remained sluggish, grain dealers in the northern U.S. grain belt said on Monday.</p>
<p>MGE Dec spring wheat closed down 1-3/4 cents at $4.05 a bushel.</p>
<p>One Montana dealer said movement was extremely slow. &quot;We are winding up the winter wheat seeding,&quot; he said.</p>
<p>The U.S. Department of Agriculture said on Monday that 90 percent of U.S. winter wheat crop had been planted versus 85 percent a week ago and 88 percent on average.</p>
<p>It said 74 percent of U.S. winter wheat had emerged, up from 63 percent a week ago and the 70 percent average.  </p>
